{
  "description": "Independent expected results for the document-quality gates. Every expectation was derived by hand from the documented rule set below, not from the implementation. Page counts are additionally cross-checked against poppler's pdfinfo at test time; byte sizes come from os.stat; word counts were counted by hand from the text shown.",
  "rule_set": {
    "format": "Detected from content signatures only. A rule passes only if the detected format is in the allowed list. Empty or unrecognised content fails a format rule.",
    "size": "Exact byte count. max_bytes N passes at <= N bytes and fails at N+1. '1 MB' without a stated basis means 1,000,000 bytes if decimal or 1,048,576 if binary: at or below 1,000,000 passes, above 1,048,576 fails, in between is unknown.",
    "pages": "PDF page-tree count. Unreadable, password-locked or corrupt PDFs are unknown, never 0. Non-PDF files are unknown for page rules.",
    "words": "whitespace_tokens: maximal runs of non-whitespace (Python str.split; NBSP splits, zero-width space does not). letters_digits_tokens: the same tokens, counting only those containing a letter or digit. Plain text with a stated convention and no exclusions is exact. PDF text, an unresolved convention, or exclusions make the count an estimate: outside the limit under every shown count fails, otherwise unknown. Scripts without spaces between words are unknown.",
    "encryption": "Any encrypted PDF fails forbid_encryption, including one that opens without a password."
  },
  "word_fixture": {
